   "body": "**Adversarial review (Claude Fable 5.1, sub-agent of ext/ezzz-opus-mp651, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head d2708ff4\n\nCode is correct, Swift 6-clean, lint-clean and mutation-tested; the two Mediums are scope/tracking, fixable in docs.\n\n1. **Medium** — `docs/lots/LOT-126-mp-list.md` (Title row). Issue scope \"Check whether the topic lists follow the same rule\" is answered nowhere. Legacy fades visited topic titles through the same `TopicListRowView`: `MainWindow.swift:655-659`, `Favorites.swift:1012`, `ForumSearchView.swift:235` @ 2440d79 pass `isVisited`; SwiftHFR `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicRowView.swift:41` changes only the weight. Fix: one line recording the gap plus a follow-up issue, or `Refs #651` naming it as left.\n2. **Medium** — PR body `Closes #651` vs LOT-126 \"Pending hand check (#651)\". The acceptance criterion requires a Mac check of the iPad selection; it is declared pending, so the issue is not fully met. Fix: run the check before merge, or `Refs #651` with what is left.\n3. **Low** — `App/SwiftHFRTests/Messages/MessageTitleToneTests.swift` never references `MessageRowView`. Scenario: delete `.foregroundStyle(titleTone.style)` at `MessageRowView.swift:38`; the suite stays green, so \"a test fails if a read title is drawn in the primary colour\" holds for the tone, not the row. Fix: render the row in `drawnColour` (fixture thread) or state the limit in the lot doc.\n4. **Low** — `MessageTitleToneTests.swift:98` samples the exact pixel between two \"█\" glyphs; an antialiased seam would blend and flake. Fix: `Rectangle().fill(tone.style)`.\n\n**Checked**\n- Legacy cites exact: `Common.swift:3118-3120`, `MPListView.swift:463-469` @ 2440d79.\n- Baseline 17/17 pass. M1 (legacy plain `.secondaryLabel` in light): `readTitleContrast(light)` and `lightUsesTheIncreasedContrastSecondary` fail. M2 (`.secondary` paints `.primary`): `drawnColour` fails both schemes. Files restored; `git status` clean.\n- Contrast claims recomputed (6:1 light at 0.8 alpha, 3.4:1 at 0.6, 15.5:1 dark+IC): match.\n- Darker/OLED, `ThemeStyle`, `darkBrightness`: reader-only, none touches list surfaces.\n- `swiftlint --strict`, `fold.py --check`: clean. Claim line matches `/claim`. LESSONS 1, 2, 3, 12, 21, 53, 54 reviewed; no security surface.\n",
   "author_association": "OWNER",
